	(text "R12 keeps a long cable from\nupsetting the op-amp.  R11 drains\nC9 so switching doesn't pop."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 160.02 119.38 0)
		(effects (font (size 1 1)) (justify left))
		(uuid "6e58ff77-735f-45dd-b39a-cba46770ef27")
	)
	(text "Gain = 1 + (U2A + wiper) / R4:  about 1.14x (+1 dB) to 10.2x (+20 dB)\nU2A is the Boost knob: the pot side of an MCP45HV51 digital pot (10k), wired as a\nvariable resistor.  Its control and power pins (U2B) are on the Digital Pot sheet.\nC3 with R4 sets the bass roll-off (about 14 Hz) and keeps the DC gain at 1."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 139.7 0)
		(effects (font (size 1 1)) (justify left))
		(uuid "d90b6996-8699-449c-92ef-da5c30de0af3")
	)
	(text "Everything is centered on VB (4.5V) so the digital pot only sees 0V to 9V.\nU1 = OPA1678 dual op-amp: U1A here, U1B buffers VB (Power sheet).\nThe breadboard uses a TL072 in its place: same pins.\nAudio-path capacitors C1, C2 and C9 must be C0G or film, not X7R."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 154.94 0)
		(effects (font (size 1 1)) (justify left))
		(uuid "bf9cf5bf-a7b6-4966-91c6-d261457f9d3a")
	)
